lth news it said  this that the plan details are available  online and it highly recommends members  to contact them to verify the benefits  the swedish hospital told cbs news that  bear was billed for the care that he  received however the surgeon advocated  to get the bill lowered since the  patient and the provider were not aware  of the lifetime limit before his surgery  joining us now is dr elizabeth rosenthal  she's the editor-in-chief of kaiser  health news good to see you dr rosenthal  can you explain this insurance policy  issue that that eli was relying on  oh yeah you know one of the wonderful  things the affordable care act did was  to impose lifetime limits in 10  essential categories but jaw surgery is  not one of them and it's in this gray  area between health insurance and  medical insurance and that's where eli  got trapped the other thing is so many  of us assume that when we see the same  name on our insurance card the policies  will work the same but what benefits you  get from any one insurance depends  largely on what your employer decides to  give you so in switching employers he  had the same looking insurance card but  the benefits were hugely different it  always seems so complicated to me that  so what can people do before and after  the surgery to avoid this happening to  them  or is there anything you can do  are you frozen  she lost her oh well i think one thing  that's really important for people  go ahead go ahead one thing that's  really important for people to know is  um you know you if you ask your doctor  is this going to be covered you know  they want it to be covered so they're  going to say sure which should be  covered by your insurance but as eli  discovered this was um on an 80-page  booklet so his doctor didn't know so  it's really important to contact your  insurer to verify those benefits the  second thing is if you don't get redress  and you get the surprise bill  you know good for eli go to your state  attorney general or your state consumer  protection  consumer protection board they may be  able to help and your doctor may be able  to help you know patients and doctors  shouldn't have to read 80 page booklets  in the fine print to just to know if  their essential surgery is going to be  covered or not you know dr elizabeth  rosenthal those 80 page booklets will  get you every single time  i don't know anybody who's reading that  stuff thank you though thank you very  much even though i know we should thank  you
 

